WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.300
<v Employee C>Hello everyone, thanks for joining. Lotte, I've also invited our Senior Expert and my colleague A.</v>

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.200
<v Lotte (Guest)>Hello, nice to meet you all.</v>

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.300
<v Senior Expert>Hello Lotte, nice to meet you. I'm the senior payroll expert for Belgium, so cross-border cases like this usually end up with me.</v>

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.200
<v Employee A>Hi Lotte, I work with C on your account.</v>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.400
<v Employee C>So, Lotte, maybe you can explain the case first?</v>

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:11.500
<v Lotte (Guest)>Of course. So at Brightwave Logistics we want to bring in a consultant from the Netherlands, Daan Visser. He's self-employed, a zelfstandige.</v>

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:21.600
<v Lotte (Guest)>He would work at our site in Mechelen for three months, starting on the twenty-second of October, at seven hundred and eighty euros a day.</v>

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.300
<v Lotte (Guest)>And we were wondering what we need to arrange on our side.</v>

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.400
<v Employee C>Thanks. And he stays registered as self-employed in the Netherlands?</v>

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.100
<v Lotte (Guest)>Yes, he has his own company there.</v>

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:33.400
<v Senior Expert>There are three things to look at. First, the Lima so declaration — it has to be done before the first working day, and you, as the client, should ask for the L1 receipt.</v>

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:40.300
<v Senior Expert>If he starts without it, the client can get into trouble too, not only him.</v>

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:49.600
<v Employee A>Yes, exactly — we had the same with a German freelancer in spring, I checked it on the Limosa portal then.</v>

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.200
<v Lotte (Guest)>Ok, I didn't know about the receipt.</v>

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:11.400
<v Senior Expert>Second, the a one certificate. He requests it from the Dutch social security office, and it shows that he stays insured in the Netherlands.</v>

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:18.300
<v Senior Expert>Without the a one, there is a risk that he has to pay contributions in both countries.</v>

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.400
<v Lotte (Guest)>Double contributions, that wouldn't make him happy.</v>

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.600
<v Senior Expert>No. So ask him for it early, it can take a few weeks.</v>

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.400
<v Lotte (Guest)>To be honest, we always handle the Limosa ourselves, it's never been a problem.</v>

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.000
<v Employee C>That's good to hear.</v>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:09.200
<v Lotte (Guest)>One more thing: our team manager would like him to work fixed hours, nine to five, and report to the team every day.</v>

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:21.300
<v Senior Expert>Ok, that's an important point. That sounds more like an employee than a freelancer — that's the schijn zelf standig heid risk, bogus self-employment.</v>

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:33.500
<v Senior Expert>Internally, our rule is: whenever a client sets fixed hours or gives instructions to a freelancer, the case is flagged to a Senior Expert before the contract is signed.</v>

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:39.300
<v Senior Expert>So C, please flag this one to me formally, and we'll look at the contract together.</v>

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.000
<v Employee C>Will do.</v>

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.400
<v Employee C>So if I understand correctly, we need the L1 and the a one before day one?</v>

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.000
<v Senior Expert>Exactly.</v>

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.200
<v Lotte (Guest)>Ok, that's clear for me.</v>

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:09.400
<v Employee C>So next steps: Lotte, you ask Daan for the a one and the Limosa receipt, and I send you a summary by e-mail.</v>

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:12.400
<v Lotte (Guest)>Perfect. Thank you all.</v>

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:16.200
<v Senior Expert>You're welcome. Good luck with the project.</v>

00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.300
<v Employee C>Thanks everyone, bye.</v>
